    <string name="about_intro">Nubo shows the forecast anywhere in the world, and the official weather warnings of Spain.</string>
    <string name="about_data">Data</string>
    <string name="about_data_forecast">Forecast — Open-Meteo. Hour by hour for the next 24 hours and a summary for seven days: temperature, apparent temperature, dew point, precipitation and its probability, wind, humidity and UV index.</string>
    <string name="about_data_air">Air quality — Open-Meteo Air Quality, European index from the Copernicus atmosphere service (CAMS). Its model runs out around the fifth day, which is why the last days show no value.</string>
    <string name="about_data_alerts">Warnings — AEMET, Spain only. They are matched by warning zone, which is smaller than a province: an inland town does not get the coastal warnings of its own province.</string>
    <string name="about_data_places">Places — Open-Meteo geocoding for search; BigDataCloud resolves the name of your current location.</string>
    <string name="about_data_astro">Sun and Moon — computed on the phone, without network, in the time zone of each city.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_body">No account, no advertising and no analytics. Your cities are stored on the phone; only their coordinates travel, to the providers above, to fetch the data you see.</string>
    <string name="about_updates">Updates</string>
    <string name="about_updates_body">Nubo is distributed outside Google Play: it checks its GitHub releases and installs the new version itself.</string>
